{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1478876-so-dragons-at-higher-power-levels","id":1478876,"title":"So, dragons at higher power levels?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-04-14T17:43:23-07:00","id":1478876,"title":"So, dragons at higher power levels?","content":"Question about the Dragon book coming out next year. I know your characters are the descendants of dragons who have draconic powers and magic and stuff, and are acting out their ancestors' will, but like what if you decided to do other stuff, like tell yer ancestor to go screw themselves and join with the gods or titans? How would playing an Heir wok in a group of scions at higher levels, like demigod and god? Could your character potentially become a full dragon or even a dragon-god? I am so interested and have so many questions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12517-storyteller323","name":"Storyteller323","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-14T18:37:41-07:00","id":1478882,"title":"","content":"Yes, Heirs have counterparts to Demigod and God levels. IIRC, they're \u201cLesser Wyrm\u201d and \u201cGreater Wyrm\u201d. And I <i>think</i> they're also able to join Pantheons \u2014 though I suspect that \u201cinfiltrate\u201d might bea more accurate term.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-14T21:07:56-07:00","id":1478889,"title":"","content":"What sort of powers do Heirs have anyways? Is it like, functionally a fancy kind of pantheon? Different mechanics? How do they take into account stuff like draconic transformation and purviews and the physical features of a dragon like wings?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12517-storyteller323","name":"Storyteller323","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-14T21:25:02-07:00","id":1478890,"title":"","content":"They have Dragon Magic: Animal Control, Decay, Elemental Manipulation (Air, Earth, Fire, Frost, or Water), Fear, Flight, Illusions, Luck, Transformation, Understanding, and Weather Control; plus Signature Dragon Magic for each Flight. They also have Transformation Knacks that gradually make them more draconian as they increase their Inheritance, in addition to their Calling Knacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-15T04:50:56-07:00","id":1478899,"title":"","content":"But, from my reading - most of Heirs mechanics are 'like Scions, only but different'. Elemental Magic is more or less Elements focused Purviews, minus ritual casting options. Transformations Knacks are Dragons-specifics Knacks, simple as such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-15-2022, 12:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-15T07:52:02-07:00","id":1478908,"title":"","content":"So for how draconic transformation works, it sounds something like at Hero level you are a human that can take on a draconic form, while at the other two levels you're a dragon that can take humanoid form? And for power, lemme see if my examples work:<br /> Inheritor - Reign of Fire.<br /> Lesser Wyrm - Smaug.<br /> Greater Wyrm - Ancalagon the Black.<br /> That seem about the right scale?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12517-storyteller323","name":"Storyteller323","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-15T08:29:35-07:00","id":1478909,"title":"","content":"I goofed; the \u201ctop level\u201d is Dragon, not \u201cGreater Wyrm\u201d. That said: yes. At the equivalent of Hero level, you're a human who can assume dragon-like aspects; and at Dragon level, you're, well, a dragon \u2014 and if you have the right Dragon Magic, you can transform into a human. I don't think that that's automatic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-15T11:24:56-07:00","id":1478916,"title":"","content":"You would think that for in game convenience it'd be a default, especially since dragons are supposed to be keeping it low key until either the titans or gods finish the other off so they can step in and fight the weakened victor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12517-storyteller323","name":"Storyteller323","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-15T17:17:13-07:00","id":1478926,"title":"","content":"Also question, say I wanted to play a draconic brawler who throws cars and rips monsters apart with his bare hands, would there be any super strength style powers inheritors have that could assist that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12517-storyteller323","name":"Storyteller323","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-16T15:44:32-07:00","id":1478979,"title":"","content":"I don't have my manuscript handy at the moment, so I can't give a precise answer; but in a similar way to how a Scion can invoke a Feat of Scale based on his Titles(?), e.g., herculean feats of might, Heirs likewise have a means of invoking Feats of Scale in ways that are appropriate for the Heir's character concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-26T11:41:02-07:00","id":1479554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Storyteller323</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1478876-so-dragons-at-higher-power-levels?p=1478926#post1478926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also question, say I wanted to play a draconic brawler who throws cars and rips monsters apart with his bare hands, would there be any super strength style powers inheritors have that could assist that?</div> </div> </div> </div>In the prerelease manuscript, it says that you have four ways to increase Scale. <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>If you are acting in coordination with your Calling, and if you have a correct Knack, you can increase your Scale by 1/2 of your Inheritance [replaces Legend] rounded up.</li> <li>If the action matches a Deed Name, you get an extra +1.</li> <li>Activate a purchased Transformation knack reflexively. Your body changes in some way.</li> <li>Imbue one Inheritance point [replaces Legend] and take a Simple action. You gain +1 Scale (doesn't stack with number 1 above; the higher value wins, so at Legend 3 it would increase) and turn into a Dragon. Whatever you want your Dragon to have, it has (claws, wings, etc). If your form has nonhuman features such as wings, you get a Complication to use it unless you've purchased a Transformation Knack.</li> </ol><br /> <br /> Example from the book: &quot;an Inheritance 4 Heir with the Iron-Fisted Rule Knack for her Judge Calling takes an action to punish someone and her Deed Name is The Writhing Punisher of Prey, she can invoke her Knack of Scale to gain +3 Scale for the action.&quot;<br /> <br /> So I create a Dragon Heir named Elspeth N\u00ed\u00f0h\u00f6ggrsdottir (Lindwurm Flight). I choose the Callings Destroyer,Predator,and Nomad. As a starting character, Elspeth gets 2 Draconic Knacks. She takes one from Scale and one from Transformation.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">For the Scale knack, I choose Destroyer: &quot;<b>Unstoppable Force</b>.&quot; Elspeth Scale equal to half her Inheritance (rounded up) when fighting a massive force.<br /> For the Transformation Knack I take &quot;<b>Massive Beast Shape</b>.&quot; Elspeth gains +1 Size and the same Scale for Feats of Strength or Stamina.<br /> I give her the Deed Name &quot;Wolfsbane&quot;.</div> <br /> When confronting an army of werewolf Titanspawn, Elspeth has two options:<br /> Human-mode:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Elspeth can gain +1 Scale (half Inheritance rounded up) as a Feat of Scale because of <b>Unstoppable Force</b>. She can spend 1 momentum to invoke her deed name, adding +1 because she's fighting wolves. She can also gain an additional +1 Scale for strength and stamina actions by activating <b>Massive Beast Shape</b>. When she does this, she physically grows even bigger. That's +3 Scale total for a single action against wolves.</div> <br /> Dragon-mode:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">She can also imbue 1 Inheritance to transform into a dragon for a scene instead. This gives her +1 Size and +2 physical Scale. She gains another +1 for fighting wolves. That's a total of +3 Scale, for the <i>scene</i>. The only flaw is that you look like a dragon.</div> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23791-ashnak","name":"Ashnak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-27T16:10:50-07:00","id":1479610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashnak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1478876-so-dragons-at-higher-power-levels?p=1479554#post1479554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In the prerelease manuscript, it says that you have four ways to increase Scale.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>If you are acting in coordination with your Calling, and if you have a correct Knack, you can increase your Scale by 1/2 of your Inheritance [replaces Legend] rounded up.</li> <li>If the action matches a Deed Name, you get an extra +1.</li> <li>Activate a purchased Transformation knack reflexively. Your body changes in some way.</li> <li>Imbue one Inheritance point [replaces Legend] and take a Simple action. You gain +1 Scale (doesn't stack with number 1 above; the higher value wins, so at Legend 3 it would increase) and turn into a Dragon. Whatever you want your Dragon to have, it has (claws, wings, etc). If your form has nonhuman features such as wings, you get a Complication to use it unless you've purchased a Transformation Knack.</li> </ol><br /> <br /> Example from the book: &quot;an Inheritance 4 Heir with the Iron-Fisted Rule Knack for her Judge Calling takes an action to punish someone and her Deed Name is The Writhing Punisher of Prey, she can invoke her Knack of Scale to gain +3 Scale for the action.&quot;<br /> <br /> So I create a Dragon Heir named Elspeth N\u00ed\u00f0h\u00f6ggrsdottir (Lindwurm Flight). I choose the Callings Destroyer,Predator,and Nomad. As a starting character, Elspeth gets 2 Draconic Knacks. She takes one from Scale and one from Transformation.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">For the Scale knack, I choose Destroyer: &quot;<b>Unstoppable Force</b>.&quot; Elspeth Scale equal to half her Inheritance (rounded up) when fighting a massive force.<br /> For the Transformation Knack I take &quot;<b>Massive Beast Shape</b>.&quot; Elspeth gains +1 Size and the same Scale for Feats of Strength or Stamina.<br /> I give her the Deed Name &quot;Wolfsbane&quot;.</div><br /> When confronting an army of werewolf Titanspawn, Elspeth has two options:<br /> Human-mode:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Elspeth can gain +1 Scale (half Inheritance rounded up) as a Feat of Scale because of <b>Unstoppable Force</b>. She can spend 1 momentum to invoke her deed name, adding +1 because she's fighting wolves. She can also gain an additional +1 Scale for strength and stamina actions by activating <b>Massive Beast Shape</b>. When she does this, she physically grows even bigger. That's +3 Scale total for a single action against wolves.</div><br /> Dragon-mode:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">She can also imbue 1 Inheritance to transform into a dragon for a scene instead. This gives her +1 Size and +2 physical Scale. She gains another +1 for fighting wolves. That's a total of +3 Scale, for the <i>scene</i>. The only flaw is that you look like a dragon.</div><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I am sorry, I do not wish to sound rude but I am a bit rusty with the game, how do feats of scale equal mimicking Epic Strength?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12517-storyteller323","name":"Storyteller323","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-29T09:36:29-07:00","id":1479706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Storyteller323</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1478876-so-dragons-at-higher-power-levels?p=1479610#post1479610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am sorry, I do not wish to sound rude but I am a bit rusty with the game, how do feats of scale equal mimicking Epic Strength?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a Dragon. They don't have access to Purviews or Boons; All Dragon magic is Knacks (three flavors: Calling Knacks like Scions, but also Draconic Knacks: Scale Knacks that allow you to gain Scale for an action, and Transformation Knacks that let your dragon form to have draconic powers) or Rituals.<br /> <br /> So the Epic Strength Innate isn't something that a Dragon can get, except by purchasing as a Transformation Knack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23791-ashnak","name":"Ashnak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-29T11:48:49-07:00","id":1479722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashnak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1478876-so-dragons-at-higher-power-levels?p=1479706#post1479706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is a Dragon. They don't have access to Purviews or Boons; All Dragon magic is Knacks (three flavors: Calling Knacks like Scions, but also Draconic Knacks: Scale Knacks that allow you to gain Scale for an action, and Transformation Knacks that let your dragon form to have draconic powers) or Rituals.<br /> <br /> So the Epic Strength Innate isn't something that a Dragon can get, except by purchasing as a Transformation Knack.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I more meant for superhuman strength based abilities. So the knacks are dependant on scale, and can be used for lifting cars or whatnot?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12517-storyteller323",